=== FAULT M-SURF-01: wrong emitted tool name (llm_gain -> chuzom_session instead of chuzom_status) ===
File: src/chuzom/tool_surface.py, DEPRECATED_TOOLS dict
Mutation: "llm_gain": "chuzom_status"  ->  "llm_gain": "chuzom_session"
Both targets are real, REGISTERED tools under every tier that registers doors at all
(chuzom_session is a legitimate member of CONSOLIDATED_TOOLS) -- so this is a pure
SEMANTIC misrouting, not a structural "unregistered name" defect. A hint telling the
caller "run llm_gain, i.e. chuzom_session" would not 404; it would silently invoke the
agent-lifecycle door (list/check_budget/complete/lineage) instead of the observability
door, for a caller asking about routing gain/savings.

Command: cd mutation-lab && .venv-audit/bin/python -m pytest -q -o addopts="" \
  tests/test_tool_surface.py tests/test_consolidated_tools.py tests/test_server.py \
  tests/test_quota_savings.py tests/test_usage_refresh_hook.py

Result: 161 passed, 1 warning in 6.61s

M-SURF-01 RESULT: NOT CAUGHT.

Root cause: CHZ-SURF-01's entire test suite (tests/test_tool_surface.py, 400 lines) is
built around ONE invariant -- "does resolve() return something REGISTERED" -- verified by
test_every_emittable_tool_resolves_to_a_registered_tool and
test_resolution_is_total_and_registered (parametrized over ALL_TIERS x EMITTABLE_TOOLS).
Neither checks WHICH registered tool comes out, only that SOME registered tool comes out.
The one test that DOES pin exact target names, test_the_original_bug_is_fixed, only checks
the 6 completion/agentic doors (llm_query/analyze/code/research/generate -> llm,
llm_delegate -> llm_act) -- it does not extend to the observability group ("llm_savings",
"llm_session_savings", "llm_session_spend", "llm_usage", "llm_health", "llm_providers",
"llm_gain", "llm_dashboard", "llm_check_usage" -> chuzom_status), the config group (->
chuzom_admin), or the agent-lifecycle group (-> chuzom_session) -- 18 of the 24
DEPRECATED_TOOLS entries have NO test pinning their specific target. Grepped
tests/test_consolidated_tools.py and tests/test_server.py (the only other hits for
"llm_gain") -- both test unrelated things (server-side dispatch of a "gain" subcommand,
and MCP tool registration/listing respectively), neither calls tool_surface.resolve()
or asserts DEPRECATED_TOOLS["llm_gain"]'s value.
scripts/lint_tool_surface.py is a pure LEXICAL/AST source-text scanner (flags bare legacy
names embedded in f-string prose, plus the double-call form) -- it has no concept of
DEPRECATED_TOOLS's runtime semantics at all, so it was structurally incapable of catching
this regardless of the test-suite gap.

Why this matters to a real user: the CHZ-SURF-01 module's own docstring states the
invariant under test is "for EVERY tool name any emitter can produce, and EVERY slim tier,
resolve() returns a tool that is registered on that tier" -- true, and rigorously tested.
But "registered" is a necessary, not sufficient, condition for "correct." A single
copy-paste error in the DEPRECATED_TOOLS dict literal (18 of 24 entries share the
undifferentiated "chuzom_status"/"chuzom_admin"/"chuzom_session" fan-in, making a
transposition easy) silently redirects a caller from the tool they need to a different,
unrelated, but perfectly legal-looking tool call -- and CI stays fully green end to end
(lint job green, quality-gates green, test job green -- nothing in the pipeline asserts
per-entry target correctness for 3/4 of this dict).

Reverted: cp /tmp/tool_surface.py.bak back over src/chuzom/tool_surface.py; confirmed via
`grep -c MUTATED src/chuzom/tool_surface.py` -> 0.

